From 2282ab644e4bf1ef948419ba69e5d5c433b68ffc Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: NeoTech <andreas@roughedge.se>
Date: Fri, 20 Nov 2026 11:40:22 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] build(kernel): remove truck-stepio, ruststep and
 truck-topology; the STEP bench reads recorded truck verdicts

Part 3 of #917. No code of the workspace reads STEP through truck any
more, so the STEP crates of truck leave the manifests and the lock:

- root Cargo.toml: the truck-stepio, truck-topology and ruststep pins,
  the #887 [patch.crates-io] git pin of ruststep and its rationale.
- crates/kernel: the bench dev-dependencies truck-stepio, truck-meshalgo,
  truck-topology and ruststep. The `truck` feature (TruckKernel) stays;
  its removal is #2922.
- Cargo.lock: ruststep, ruststep-derive, truck-stepio, Inflector,
  derive-new and the old duplicates itertools 0.10.5, proc-macro-crate
  1.3.1, toml_edit 0.19.15, toml_datetime 0.6.11, winnow 0.5.40.

The truck side of the STEP bench is a recorded reading now
(tests/step_agreement/rows.rs), taken from the bench's own printout at
4b694c7c7. The live solidcore reading is judged against it by the same
rules, and every pinned verdict is unchanged. step_agreement.rs is split
along its seam (rows, verdicts, tests; #2800). The truck-only test of
step_import.rs is replaced by recorded_truck_readings_keep_their_findings;
the #[test] count of the crate is the same. The printed-only truck column
of the mesh deviation bench is dropped. Stale comments and the truck
license notices follow.

Refs #27
Refs #2922
Fixes #2800
Fixes #2790
Fixes #917

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
